    <div class="stack" style="margin-top: 16px;">
      <details class="faq"><summary>How is a vCISO different from a full-time CISO?</summary><p>You get the same executive-level direction and accountability, but on a flexible engagement sized to your stage and budget — instead of a single permanent salary and the time it takes to recruit one.</p></details>
      <details class="faq"><summary>Can a vCISO help us pass SOC 2 or ISO 27001?</summary><p>Yes. Readiness is a core deliverable: gap analysis, policy creation, control implementation guidance, and the documentation auditors expect. We prepare the program; the certification audit itself is performed by an independent assessor.</p></details>
      <details class="faq"><summary>Do we have to use AEGIS PDNS?</summary><p>No. The vCISO engagement stands on its own. Where protective DNS is a prioritized control, AEGIS PDNS is an easy, transparent option to fold in — but it is never required.</p></details>
